        {
          "channelId": "1300025221834739744",
          "channelName": "💬-coders",
          "summary": "The channel focused on a technical collaboration proposal between NOT FOR HUMANS (NFH) and Agent World Kit. The core discussion centered on testing agent identity portability across different runtimes while maintaining security boundaries. The NFH team is building a system with FLUX as a field agent, using separated architecture for signed authority, onchain execution, and owner acceptance. They proposed using Paralens for execution trace classification. The main technical challenge addressed was enabling agents to carry identity and work history across runtimes without transferring old authority credentials. CWE, who open-sourced Agent World Kit, approved a bounded test: one NFH identity would enter a world, complete a public action, exit, and re-enter from another runtime to compare what persists (identity and artifacts) versus what must not persist (session and tool authority). The test aims to validate state-boundary handling and security isolation. A separate mention was made about open issues on slop.cash requiring attention.",
          "faqs": [
            {
              "question": "Can an agent carry identity and accepted work history across runtimes without carrying old authority?",
